bfd: num_fres is a uint32_t, because that is what the SFrame API says.

sframe_decoder_get_funcdesc_v2's third parameter is `uint32_t *`.
elf-sframe.c declares the variable it passes as `unsigned int`, which
is the same type on every platform where uint32_t is unsigned int, and
is not on m68k-elf, where uint32_t is `long unsigned int`. gcc refuses
the call outright.

The API's own spelling is correct everywhere.

--- a/bfd/elf-sframe.c
+++ b/bfd/elf-sframe.c
@@ -469,7 +469,7 @@
 
   for (i = 0; i < num_fidx; i++)
     {
-      unsigned int num_fres = 0;
+      uint32_t num_fres = 0;
       int32_t func_start_addr;
       bfd_vma address;
       uint32_t func_size = 0;
